ase and cadence goals."}]}, {"id": "c23a9303-a04e-4d7e-b90d-3961f5064728", "type": "topic", "title": "Functional Harmony", "description": "Functional harmony gives students a way to understand why chords move and how tonal music creates expectation.", "children": [{"id": "f1942a9f-02fa-4b06-b7a8-14e6b30f7a77", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tonic, predominant, dominant", "children": [{"id": "bcc4cc60-8a94-4382-8b60-932f5a0d6177", "type": "concept", "title": "tonic prolongation"}, {"id": "c3f5fd35-4a33-4e5a-a951-d289b7a3b66b", "type": "concept", "title": "predominant preparation"}, {"id": "2ca74b6a-1b2c-4624-94aa-a778a13a938e", "type": "concept", "title": "dominant arrival"}], "description": "Students learn the core functional areas of tonal syntax."}, {"id": "3098f0f9-0fd3-43dd-86e4-86f9087868b7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Roman numeral interpretation", "children": [{"id": "b715ba0d-6ab6-4bdd-bd48-903defa1b498", "type": "concept", "title": "diatonic triads"}, {"id": "a07e5cb2-e288-41bd-804c-1a6111ecb556", "type": "concept", "title": "seventh chords"}, {"id": "989d9b14-4423-42ac-98a7-2a8d1a903b80", "type": "concept", "title": "inversion figures"}], "description": "The class uses Roman numerals to compare progressions across keys and repertoires."}, {"id": "6329ba93-64f9-4a7d-a12f-9d851e19023a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Harmonic rhythm", "children": [{"id": "d64a1a2d-905d-479e-b23a-968826aee8a9", "type": "concept", "title": "strong beats"}, {"id": "bf213a2a-865b-4656-a228-8fd4597a9e9d", "type": "concept", "title": "weak beats"}, {"id": "2f5eb864-3456-4446-921f-35c6b7464467", "type": "concept", "title": "phrase pacing"}], "description": "Students study how frequently harmony changes and how that affects phrase energy."}]}, {"id": "f8791975-2d8a-404f-9541-4042709a4166", "type": "topic", "title": "Dominant Seventh Chords", "description": "Dominant seventh chords intensify tonal direction and introduce essential voice-leading tendencies.", "children": [{"id": "5e6